{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/8744-side-stepping-ragnarok-minor-spoilers-from-ragnarok-book","id":8744,"title":"Side-stepping Ragnarok **minor spoilers from Ragnarok book**","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-12T05:58:45-08:00","id":8744,"title":"Side-stepping Ragnarok **minor spoilers from Ragnarok book**","content":"So I just ran a (heavily) modified opening story arc from the Ragnarok book. I cliffhangered it and let the impact of the situation sink in.<br /> If you are playing in the arc and don't know the specifics, look away now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Aftr the game, a few players were looking up specifics on Ragnarok (they're knowledgeable on Greek and Japanese, but only one of them with Norse myths). They found that the Jotunhammer is not really a thing. In a desperate bid to avoid Ragnarok, they have taken an odd logical stance: &quot;Fimbulvetr lasts for 3 years. If this does not last 3 years, it is not Fimbulvetr.&quot;<br /> <br /> I have already told them that they cannot go into the past and stop the Jotunhammer. Barring that, I almost want them to try and figure out a way to side-step the plot. The trick is that I am only going to give them one year to do this. If it ticks past Mar 2015 (game is in current time) -Ragnarok is back on. I would think that, to remove a dust cloud of that size and density, it would take an avatar of Ehekatoyaatl or, to burn it away, Muspelheim. I am not letting the heroes skip the Fate of the Gods without at least freeing an Aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T02:13:15-08:00","id":9534,"title":"","content":"I'm not really familiar with the book in question. Is it a plot book leading up to Ragnarok similar to the End of Days WW did for the oWoD? Or is it a story about stopping Ragnarok?<br /> <br /> I'm just curious. In Norse mythology, the inevitability of prophecy is a pretty central tenet. In other words, if something has been foretold, it cannot be avoided (there's a story that emphasise this, about a wealthy farmer who is prophesied to be killed by his own horse. Trying to avoid his fate, he has the horse killed and the remains buried. The story ends with the summary &quot;he lived to be 300 years old, before finally meeting his prophesied end.&quot;) Prophecy is a dangerous thing to play around with in Norse mythology. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This also means that, if playing strictly by the mythology, that Ragnarok cannot be stopped. It has been foretold, so it <i>will</i> happen. But as the farmer's story, it can certainly be postponed and by mythological logic, your players are essentially right.<br /> <br /> Anyway. I don't really know where I'm going with this. Sounds like a cool game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/635-slaunyeh","name":"Slaunyeh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T13:35:04-08:00","id":11536,"title":"","content":"Only one scion in the band is from the Aesir. The rest of the scions really don't want to deal with Ragnarok. So much so, in fact, that they are beginning an assault on Zrvan to try and 'convince' at least one of the aspects (Chronos) to aid them in sending at least one of them back in time to prevent the destruction. Now all they have to do is determine how the Jotunhammer was brought forth....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T23:02:29-08:00","id":11912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/8744-side-stepping-ragnarok-minor-spoilers-from-ragnarok-book?p=11536#post11536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only one scion in the band is from the Aesir. The rest of the scions really don't want to deal with Ragnarok. So much so, in fact, that they are beginning an assault on Zrvan to try and 'convince' at least one of the aspects (Chronos) to aid them in sending at least one of them back in time to prevent the destruction. Now all they have to do is determine how the Jotunhammer was brought forth....</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's the direction they want to go; let them. Part of the insanity of Scion is seeing how the heroes strive to achieve Great Things and hey, maybe they avert Ragnarok. HOORAY ... now throw something even MORE horrible at them; like the release of Greater Titans all at once or the released Titan Aspect coming to them for more and more deals to blackmail the players. If they don't agree, he revokes the time-loop.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T15:39:42-08:00","id":12337,"title":"","content":"I was thinking of reversing most of the good deeds they have done up to this point (Chronos' take on &quot;Put things right&quot;). Seeing as they had already put down a mokkurkalfi to stop it from waking Jormungander, as well as prevented titanspawn from obtaining the key to Ggantija (used as a secret entrance to the Overworld), things may get really fun, really quick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T15:42:51-08:00","id":12340,"title":"","content":"I forgot about the hyper-intelligent squirrel that was using forbidden magics to turn everyone in Canada into wendigos.<br /> (This is what happens when you mix the Axiom knack with Maccallan 25)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","user":"PHGraves","date":".  Always have a Designated Storyteller, kids. 11-16-2013, 06:4